# DOM Concursos — Agent Rules

## What is this project?
DOM Concursos is an all-in-one study platform for Brazilian public competitions (concursos públicos).
Built with Next.js, Supabase, Tailwind CSS v4, and shadcn/ui (Radix).
I am the sole developer. The codebase must be clean, consistent, and easy for future developers to understand.

---

## Tech Stack
- **Framework:** Next.js 15 (App Router)
- **Database & Auth:** Supabase (PostgreSQL)
- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS v4 + shadcn/ui (Radix)
- **Hosting:** Vercel
- **Automation:** N8N
- **AI:** Open AI
- **Language:** TypeScript (strict)

---

## Language Rules
- All UI text, labels, buttons, placeholders, messages, and content must be in **Portuguese (PT-BR)**
- All code (variables, functions, components, files, types) must be in **English**
- Database table and column names are in **English**
- Comments in code can be in English or Portuguese — be consistent within the same file

---

## Folder Structure
```
src/
├── app/
│   ├── (auth)/          → login, register pages
│   ├── (student)/       → all student-facing pages
│   ├── (admin)/         → admin panel pages
│   └── layout.tsx       → root layout
├── components/
│   ├── ui/              → base shadcn/ui components
│   ├── layout/          → Navbar, Sidebar, Footer, etc.
│   └── shared/          → reusable feature components
├── lib/
│   ├── supabase/        → supabase client, server, middleware
│   └── utils/           → helper functions
├── hooks/               → custom React hooks
├── types/               → TypeScript type definitions
└── styles/              → globals.css
```

---

## Naming Conventions
- **Files:** kebab-case → `course-card.tsx`, `use-auth.ts`
- **Components:** PascalCase → `CourseCard`, `LessonPlayer`
- **Functions & variables:** camelCase → `getCourses()`, `isLoading`
- **Types & interfaces:** PascalCase → `Course`, `UserProfile`
- **Database tables/columns:** snake_case English → `lesson_progress`, `user_id`
- **CSS classes:** Tailwind utility classes only — no custom CSS unless absolutely necessary

---

## Styling Rules
- Always use the design tokens defined in `src/app/globals.css`
- Never use hardcoded colors like `#C9A84C` or `hsl(...)` directly in components
- Always use semantic Tailwind classes that reference CSS variables:
  ```tsx
  // ✅ correct
  className="bg-background text-foreground"
  className="bg-card border-border"
  className="text-primary bg-primary/10"

  // ❌ wrong
  className="bg-[#0B1220] text-[#EEF1F8]"
  className="bg-yellow-500"
  ```
- The design is **dark mode by default** — `:root` already has dark colors
- Use `bg-background`, `bg-card`, `bg-muted`, `bg-sidebar` for layered backgrounds
- Use `text-foreground`, `text-muted-foreground` for text hierarchy
- Use `border-border` for all borders
- Use `bg-primary` and `text-primary` for gold accent elements (CTAs, highlights)
- Use `bg-accent` and `text-accent` for blue accent elements (links, active states)
- Use `bg-destructive` for errors and delete actions
- Border radius: always use `rounded-lg` (--radius-lg) for cards, `rounded-full` for pills/badges
- Always use icon library components (e.g. `lucide-react`) for UI icons
- Never use inline SVG markup for icons
- Never use Unicode symbols or emojis as UI icons

---

## Component Rules
- Every component must be typed with TypeScript — no `any`
- Add `'use client'` only when the component uses hooks, state, or browser events
- Server components are preferred by default (no `'use client'` unless needed)
- Always use `next/image` instead of `<img>` tags
- Always use `next/link` instead of `<a>` tags for internal navigation

---

## Supabase Rules
- Always use the server-side Supabase client for data fetching in Server Components
- Always use the browser-side Supabase client for mutations in Client Components
- Never expose the `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` on the client side
- Row Level Security (RLS) must be enabled on all tables
- Always handle Supabase errors explicitly — never silently ignore them:
  ```ts
  const { data, error } = await supabase.from('courses').select()
  if (error) throw new Error(error.message) //or use toast if imported
  ```

---

## Page & Route Rules
- Student pages live under `app/(student)/`
- Admin pages live under `app/(admin)/`
- Auth pages live under `app/(auth)/`
- Each route group has its own `layout.tsx` with its own navigation
- Use loading.tsx and error.tsx files for each route segment
- Always protect student and admin routes — check session in layout or middleware

---

## Platform Context
- Target audience: Brazilian students preparing for public competitions
- "Banca" = exam organization (CESPE, FCC, VUNESP, etc.)
- "Simulado" = mock exam that simulates real competition
- "Apostila" = study booklet/PDF
- "Edital" = official competition announcement
- "Matéria" = subject (e.g. Direito Constitucional)
- "Assunto" = specific topic within a subject
- Free lessons → YouTube embed
- Premium lessons → Panda Video embed
- Access control is via `profiles.access_level = 'free' | 'premium'`

---

## Code Quality Rules
- No `console.log` in production code — use proper error handling
- No commented-out code blocks — delete unused code
- No hardcoded user IDs, API keys, or secrets in code — use `.env.local`
- Keep components small and focused — if a component exceeds ~150 lines, split it
- Reuse components from `components/shared/` before creating new ones
- Always add loading and empty states to data-fetching components

---

## Width and Height Rules

Due to a Tailwind v4 issue with arbitrary values, never use 
Tailwind classes for fixed widths and heights.

ALWAYS use inline style for:
- Fixed widths: style={{ width: '280px', minWidth: '280px' }}
- Fixed heights: style={{ height: '300px' }}
- Both together: style={{ width: '280px', height: '300px' }}

NEVER use these Tailwind classes:
- w-[280px], h-[300px], min-w-[280px], max-w-[280px]
- Any arbitrary value with brackets for width or height

Use Tailwind ONLY for:
- Colors: bg-card, text-foreground, border-border
- Spacing: p-4, px-5, py-3, gap-4, m-2
- Border radius: rounded-xl, rounded-2xl
- Flex/Grid: flex, grid, flex-col, items-center, justify-between
- Hover/transitions: hover:border-primary/40, transition-colors
- Typography: text-sm, font-bold, line-clamp-2

Examples:

CORRECT:
<div
  style={{ width: '280px', minWidth: '280px', height: '300px' }}
  className="bg-card rounded-2xl border border-border p-4"
>

WRONG:
<div className="w-[280px] min-w-[280px] h-[300px] bg-card rounded-2xl">